   194	# Gate results
   195	
   196	## Gate A — PASS
   197	
   198	- **A1:** The entry claim contains the same constructor-level body as
   199	  `solution.mpy`; all program-defined code executes under fixed semantics.
   200	  The count-two body mutation invalidates the loop theorem.
   201	- **A2:** No operational bridge skips state. The claims account for result
   202	  allocation, heap append updates, scope changes, return state, call stack,
   203	  exceptions, and exit code.
   204	- **A3:** Module and local bindings, callee/argument evaluation, loop control,
   205	  method dispatch, return, and frame cleanup execute under the supplied rules.
   206	  The loop theorem quantifies over exactly the continuation it accepts.
   207	- **A4:** The two proof-local functions have exhaustive, nonoverlapping,
   208	  descending equations. No false global equation or opaque value is present.
   209	- **A5:** `[1]` is a realizable `allInts` witness. The false `[]`
   210	  postcondition is rejected and exposes the actual `[1]` result.
   211	
   212	## Gate B — PASS
   213	
   214	- **B1:** `allInts(INPUT)` matches `List[int]`; no length, sign, distinctness,
   215	  or magnitude restriction is added.
   216	- **B2:** For this domain the supplied model uses unbounded integers, integer
   217	  equality, finite list order, `count`, and `append` consistently with the
   218	  relevant Python behavior. The input is represented as the semantics'
   219	  documented unboxed read-only list value; this function never mutates it.
   220	- **B3:** The `rdAcc` equations are the keep-exactly-once, original-order
   221	  property itself, not an opaque execution summary.
   222	- **B4:** The implementation and property align formally and in all recorded
   223	  concrete tests.
   224	
   225	## Gate C — PASS
   226	
   227	- **C1:** The trust ledger below names all components outside the theorem and
   228	  their effects.
   229	- **C2:** `smoke.py`, `smoke.mpy`, `differential_test.py`,
   230	  `spec-vacuity.k`, `spec-body-mutation.k`, `prove.sh`, and
   231	  `prove-run.out` exist and reproduce the reported evidence.
   232	- **C3:** Formal results, finite evidence, trust assumptions, and exclusions
   233	  are separated here. `#Top` is reported only as proof execution, not by
