   246	
   247	# Empirical evidence
   248	
   249	`smoke.py` runs the empty list, singleton, prompt example, all-duplicate, and
   250	negative/zero/mixed-multiplicity cases through LLVM `krun`.
   251	
   252	`differential_test.py` uses `collections.Counter`, independently of
   253	`list.count` and `rdAcc`. It checks every sequence of lengths 0 through 6 over
   254	`{-2,-1,0,1,2}` (19,531 cases), then 2,000 deterministic random integer lists
   255	of lengths 0 through 40 over `[-100,100]`. It found zero mismatches. These are
   256	finite adequacy observations, not a universal proof.
   257	
   258	# Excluded behavior
   259	
